-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
tools/country-shapes/  —  the silhouette artwork
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Source:    Unknown.
Retrieved: 2026-09-08, by a crawl whose origin was not recorded.
License:   Unknown. No licence, terms or attribution accompanied the files, and
           none is stated inside them.

    Every silhouette the game shows is traced from these 196 drawings (D-69).
    This entry exists because a reader deserves the true answer about where the
    artwork came from, and the true answer is that nobody wrote it down.

    They were kept out of the build for ten days for exactly that reason
    (D-15, D-16). D-69 reversed it: Natural Earth at 10m draws Nauru with nine
    vertices and Monaco with twelve, and the silhouettes it produced were not
    good enough to play. The files are committed under tools/country-shapes/
    rather than left in the gitignored assets/ directory so that the unknown is
    visible rather than hidden, and so a clean clone can run the build.

    If you are reusing this repository: this directory, and the derived file
    backend/functions/src/data/shapes.json, are the one part of it whose
    redistribution terms nobody can vouch for. Everything else here is
    accounted for above.

    Only the OUTLINE comes from here. Every centroid, and therefore every
    distance and compass hint the game gives, still comes from Natural Earth.
    tools/lib/artwork.mjs applies D-8, fits the result into the same 500x500
    box, and simplifies to a pixel tolerance; the drawings are not modified
    beyond that and coordinate rounding.


