-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Wikimedia Commons  —  the photographs themselves
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Source:   https://commons.wikimedia.org
License:  per file. tools/build-people.mjs keeps only files whose Commons
          `License` is public domain, CC0, CC BY or CC BY-SA, and records each
          file's author and licence alongside it.

The photographs are NOT redistributed: each is fetched by the player's browser
from commons.wikimedia.org, and the author and licence are shown under it while
the challenge is on screen. Where Commons names no author, the credit reads what
Commons reads, usually "Unknown author".


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Wikipédia (pt)  —  one paragraph on who each person was
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Source:   https://pt.wikipedia.org
License:  CC BY-SA 4.0  —  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

Unlike the photographs, this text IS redistributed: the lead paragraph of each
article is vendored into backend/functions/src/data/people.json at build time by
tools/build-people.mjs and served from here. 989 of the 1,013 people have one.

The licence is honoured where the text is shown, which is only ever the reveal
of a finished challenge: the paragraph carries a link to the article it came
from and a line naming CC BY-SA 4.0, and neither half is ever rendered without
the other. The text is used unmodified apart from being cut to a sentence
boundary to fit under the photograph.
